WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.280
Test 2. This is the IELTS listening test. You will hear a number of different recordings

00:00:07.280 --> 00:00:12.600
and you will have to answer questions on what you hear. There will be time for you to read

00:00:12.600 --> 00:00:18.280
the instructions and questions and you will have a chance to check your work. All the

00:00:18.280 --> 00:00:25.719
recordings will be played once only. The test is in four parts. At the end of the test,

00:00:25.719 --> 00:00:31.559
you will be given ten minutes to transfer your answers to the answer sheet. Now turn

00:00:31.559 --> 00:00:41.160
to part one. Part one. You will hear a man asking about

00:00:41.160 --> 00:00:47.000
voluntary work in the village that he has just moved to. First, you have some time to

00:00:47.000 --> 00:00:49.360
look at questions one to seven.

00:01:17.000 --> 00:01:38.000
Hello. Jane Fairbank speaking. Oh, good morning. My name's Frank Pritchard.

00:01:38.000 --> 00:01:44.199
I've just retired and moved to Southo. I'd like to become a volunteer and I gather you

00:01:44.199 --> 00:01:48.599
coordinate voluntary work in the village? That's right.

00:01:48.599 --> 00:01:53.800
What sort of thing could I do? Well, we need help with the village library.

00:01:53.800 --> 00:02:00.680
We borrow books from the town library and individuals also donate them. So one thing

00:02:00.680 --> 00:02:06.720
you could do is get involved in collecting them, if you've got a car that is.

00:02:06.720 --> 00:02:12.020
Yes, that's no problem. The times are pretty flexible so we can arrange

00:02:12.059 --> 00:02:18.860
it to suit you. Oh, another thing is the records that we keep of the books we're given and

00:02:18.860 --> 00:02:24.380
those we borrow and need to return to the town library. It would be very useful to have

00:02:24.380 --> 00:02:31.139
another person to help keep them up to date. Right. I'm used to working on a computer.

00:02:31.139 --> 00:02:35.020
I presume they're computerised? Oh, yes.

00:02:35.020 --> 00:02:40.339
Is the library purpose built? I haven't noticed it when I've walked around the village.

00:02:40.339 --> 00:02:47.100
No, we simply have the use of a room in the village hall. The West Room. It's on the left

00:02:47.100 --> 00:02:51.100
as you go in. I must go and have a look inside the hall.

00:02:51.100 --> 00:02:56.179
Yes, it's a nice building. Do you run a lunch club in the village for

00:02:56.179 --> 00:03:03.179
elderly people? I know a lot of places do. Yes, we have a very successful club.

00:03:03.179 --> 00:03:06.580
I could help with transport, if that's of any use.

00:03:06.580 --> 00:03:12.279
Oh, definitely. People come to the club from neighbouring villages and we're always in

00:03:12.279 --> 00:03:17.139
need of more drivers. And does the club have groups that focus on

00:03:17.139 --> 00:03:23.979
a particular hobby too? I could get involved in one or two, particularly if there are any

00:03:23.979 --> 00:03:28.899
art groups. Excellent. I'll find out where we need help

00:03:28.899 --> 00:03:35.100
and get back to you. Fine. What about help for individual residents?

00:03:35.100 --> 00:03:41.740
Do you arrange that at all? Yes, we do it as a one-off. Oh, in fact, there's

00:03:41.740 --> 00:03:49.300
Mrs Carroll. She needs a lift to the hospital next week and we're struggling to find someone.

00:03:49.300 --> 00:03:54.460
When's her appointment? On Tuesday. It would take the whole morning.

00:03:54.460 --> 00:03:59.419
I could do that. Oh, that would be great. Thank you. And also

00:03:59.419 --> 00:04:06.059
next week, we're arranging to have some work done to Mr Salisbury's house before he moves,

00:04:06.059 --> 00:04:12.179
as he isn't healthy enough to do it himself. We've got some people to decorate his kitchen.

00:04:12.179 --> 00:04:16.779
But if you could do some weeding in his garden, that would be wonderful.

00:04:16.779 --> 00:04:22.980
OK, I'd enjoy that. And presumably the day and time are flexible?

00:04:22.980 --> 00:04:28.859
Oh yes. Just say when would suit you best and we'll let Mr Salisbury know.

00:04:28.980 --> 00:04:29.980
Good.

00:04:33.380 --> 00:04:39.380
Before you hear the rest of the conversation, you have some time to look at questions 8 to 10.

00:04:54.059 --> 00:04:57.579
Now listen and answer questions 8 to 10.

00:04:59.859 --> 00:05:07.859
The Volunteers Group also organises monthly social events, which is a great way to meet other people, of course.

00:05:07.859 --> 00:05:08.859
Uh-huh.

00:05:08.859 --> 00:05:18.859
So next month, on the 19th October, we're holding a quiz. A couple of residents are great at planning unusual ones,

00:05:18.859 --> 00:05:21.859
and we always fill the village hall.

00:05:21.859 --> 00:05:25.859
That sounds like fun. Can I do anything to help?

00:05:25.859 --> 00:05:32.859
Well, because of the number of people, we need plenty of refreshments for halfway through.

00:05:32.859 --> 00:05:35.859
So if you could provide any, we'd be grateful.

00:05:35.859 --> 00:05:40.859
I'm sure I could. I'll think about what to make and let you know.

00:05:40.859 --> 00:05:41.859
Thank you.

00:05:41.859 --> 00:05:48.859
Then on November the 18th, we're holding a dance, also in the village hall.

00:05:48.859 --> 00:05:58.859
We've booked a band that specialises in music of the 1930s. They've been before, and we've had a lot of requests to bring them back.

00:05:58.859 --> 00:06:03.859
I'm not really a dancer, but I'd like to do something to help.

00:06:03.859 --> 00:06:12.859
Well, we sell tickets in advance, and having an extra person to check them at the door as people arrive would be good.

00:06:12.859 --> 00:06:16.859
It can be quite a bottleneck if everyone arrives at once.

00:06:16.859 --> 00:06:18.859
OK, I'm happy with that.

00:06:18.859 --> 00:06:25.859
We're also arranging a New Year's Eve party. We're expecting that to be a really big event,

00:06:25.859 --> 00:06:30.859
so instead of the village hall, it'll be held in the Mountfort Hotel.

00:06:30.859 --> 00:06:31.859
The...?

00:06:31.859 --> 00:06:42.859
Mountfort. M-O-U-N-T-F-O-R-T Hotel.

00:06:42.859 --> 00:06:47.859
It isn't in Southow itself, but it's only a couple of miles away.

00:06:47.859 --> 00:06:52.859
The hotel will be providing dinner, and we've booked a band.

00:06:52.859 --> 00:06:59.859
The one thing we haven't got yet is a poster. That isn't something you could do by any chance, is it?

00:06:59.859 --> 00:07:06.859
Well, actually, yes. Before I retired, I was a graphic designer, so that's right up my street.

00:07:06.859 --> 00:07:12.859
Oh, perfect. I'll give you the details, and then perhaps you could send me a draft?

00:07:12.859 --> 00:07:13.859
Of course.

00:07:36.859 --> 00:07:41.859
Thank you for watching!

